From: BK7258 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] netdb: allow configurations with only RPMsg sockets

getaddrinfo() and rexec_af() already support AF_RPMSG.  Requiring an IP
family prevents a CP with only RPMsg sockets from building the standard
rexec client, which links against rexec_af().  Allow that existing backend
without enabling an unused IP stack.

Baseline: OpenVela NuttX 76354c637858ecb0aa4601629327acb6f44a26bb

diff --git a/libs/libc/netdb/Kconfig b/libs/libc/netdb/Kconfig
--- a/libs/libc/netdb/Kconfig
+++ b/libs/libc/netdb/Kconfig
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 
 config LIBC_NETDB
 	bool "netdb support"
-	depends on NET_IPv4 || NET_IPv6
+	depends on NET_IPv4 || NET_IPv6 || NET_RPMSG
 	default n
 
 menu "NETDB Support"
